;; world/rooms/glasswood/x0y5.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (0 5)
  title: "Cave Mouth"
  intent: "the caves' east end, black until you carry a light: a green stone that rings and opens as you come carrying H3, and the climb up to the scree"
  bed: (wind 0.1 water 0.5 hum 0.4 drone 0.7)
  light: 0.33
  grid:
  ("################    #####"
   "###############%    %####"
   "#        ######%    %####"
   "         ######%    %####"
   "            #  %    %####"
   "#######     #  %    %####"
   "#########   #  %    %####"
   "########### o           #"
   "#############           #"
   "#########################"
   "#########################")
  things: ((ring-stone at: (12 7) overtone: 3)
           (lantern-moth at: (18 5) count: 4 drawn: 3))
  decor: auto)
;; The dark before H3 (David, 2026-09-27, after playing b22a4d6: he never
;; found the Glass Chute's chamber, because the tree and H3 stand between it
;; and the fall). The Scree Foot's floor opens where you drop from the Scree
;; (columns 16-19), so the way in falls into this chamber: black, the moths
;; far off and not coming, and a green stone (12,7) humming A3 in the wall,
;; shivering off-key at the H2 you carry. The rough shaft (walls 15 and 20)
;; climbs back up. Carrying H3 you come to the stone from the other side,
;; along the high passage from Root Ice (rows 3-4) and down the steps: it
;; rings and opens, and the shaft is the way home.
